# =============================================================================
# OpenDDIL Edge SDK (.NET) — Cursor Rules
# =============================================================================

# Project Identity
You are working in the openddil-edge-dotnet repository — the .NET Edge SDK for
the OpenDDIL DDIL-resilient CQRS framework.

# Tech Stack (DO NOT deviate)
- Language: C# (.NET 8+)
- Database: SQLite via Microsoft.Data.Sqlite (NOT System.Data.SQLite)
- Serialization: Google.Protobuf (NOT JSON, NOT MessagePack)
- Event Contracts: Generated from openddil-contracts (NOT defined here)
- Envelope: CloudEvents v1.0 (from openddil-contracts)

# Architecture Rules
- ALL writes go through the Outbox. NEVER write directly to a network endpoint.
- The OutboxManager is the ONLY class that touches SQLite for writes.
- Domain events MUST be wrapped in a CloudEvent envelope before serialization.
- payload_bytes stores the FULL CloudEvent (envelope + packed payload), not just the domain event.

# Coding Style
- PascalCase for public methods and properties.
- camelCase for private fields with underscore prefix (_connection).
- XML doc comments on all public members.
- Async/await for I/O operations in production code.
- IDisposable pattern for database connections.

# Operation Wrappers
- Each bounded context gets its own Operations class (e.g., InventoryOperations).
- Operations classes take OutboxManager + userId in constructor.
- Operations methods construct the domain event, call Enqueue(), and return the event ID.
- Operations methods MUST accept the current read-cache value for conflict detection fields.

# Safety
- NEVER make network calls from the Edge SDK. The Relay handles all network I/O.
- NEVER modify the Outbox schema without updating both Edge SDK repos symmetrically.
- NEVER skip the CloudEvent envelope — HQ processors depend on it.
